A||||6||William Federle||1984 throttle posn sensor||||5
Z||000000||William Federle||10-28-1999||07:00 AM||||Can anyone tell me if there is a way to adjust the throttle position sensor. I was <BR>reading in the Chilton manual - the new one -<BR>that it should be adjusted after installation<BR>but looking at it I can't see any adjustment.<BR>Is there a way to adjust the throttle shaft<BR>to get the required output from the sensor?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||10-28-1999||09:06 AM||||TPS is not adjustable. The manual test is just to make sure the new one is installed and operating correctly. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||William Federle||10-28-1999||09:55 AM||||Thanks for the reply ogre. I learn a little<BR>bit more about this car everyday.||||reg||14
Z||000003||mwbackus||10-28-1999||10:03 AM||||Ogre, does that also apply to the V6 TPS installation?  I heard of someone bending the lever to adjust one, but that seems a bit unusual to me.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-28-1999||10:35 AM||||I haven't had the TPS off the V6, so if it has a lever..... <P>bending the lever would be the only adjustment you could make on either the V6 or the 300 TBI(4cyl). This should not be needed under any normal condition. The lever could be bent in use by forcing a failed, binding, TPS to move but that should be rare. As long as the TPS output at closed throttle is below 1.25VDC, i think, then it's working correctly. (I don't have the book handy) If you do bend the arm do so carefully. It's not intended to be an adjustment and won't take allot of abuse.<P>On the 700 TBI used from 87 on with the 4 cyl there is no lever, and no adjustment at all. It works right or its bad.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AL||10-28-1999||11:17 PM||||if memory serves me right, i think the voltage is 0.5. you need a voltmeter to read it right.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||10-29-1999||12:09 AM||||When i replaced my tps about 2 weeks ago they gave me an adjustable one.  It has slots for the screws and you rotate the whole thing to adjust the voltage up or down.  At closed throttle the voltage should be around .800, WOT should measure 5 volts.||||reg||1
